; Four flaps folded out over the rim at 35 deg. The bases are R_x(-35) on the
; front flap, R_x(+35) on the back, R_z(+35) on the right and R_z(-35) on the
; left — each one tilting its own outward axis UP, away from the mouth, so the
; box reads as opened rather than as a hole in a block.
;
; Written as ROWS, which is what a .tscn Transform3D lists and the transpose of
; what the Transform3D(x_axis, y_axis, z_axis, origin) constructor takes. These
; were checked by printing basis.x/.y/.z from a probe, not by eye: a flap on a
; symmetric box looks plausible folded the wrong way.
[node name="FlapFront" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.819152, 0.573576, 0, -0.573576, 0.819152, 0, 0.178679, 0.204958)
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_flap_z")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_card")

